✅ Story 2: Streamlined Product Authorization Management

Before:
Product authorizations had to be manually added or removed for each Test Centre and their Physical Buildings. This was time-consuming, error-prone, and inconsistent.

What We Did:

    Enabled the CMDS UI to view and configure IOP product authorizations.

    Developed functionality to configure products for both Test Centres and their PBs.

    Implemented cascade logic so product approvals at the Test Centre level now automatically apply to all associated PBs.

Impact:
Significantly reduced manual work. One configuration at the TC level now efficiently cascades to all related PBs, ensuring faster and consistent product setup.

🧾 [Jira: IOP-138, IOP-159, IOP-118, IOP-143]
✅ Story 3: Allocation Group Landing Page and Role-Based Access

Before:
There was no centralized interface to manage allocation groups, nor a system to control user access to allocation functionalities. This raised concerns over both usability and security.

What We Did:

    Built a new landing page for Allocation Groups in CMDS.

    Set up RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) to define which users can access or perform actions related to allocation groups.

    Implemented CRUD permissions to control Create, Read, Update, and Delete operations based on user roles.

Impact:
Users now have a centralized, secure, and intuitive interface to manage allocation groups, and permissions are tightly aligned with user roles to prevent unauthorized access.

🧾 [Jira: IOP-160, IOP-466, IOP-476]
✅ Story 4: Full Lifecycle Management of Allocation Groups

Before:
There was no functionality to manage allocation groups — users couldn’t create, view, or edit groups from the UI, leading to operational inefficiencies.

What We Did:

    Developed features to create new allocation groups with key inputs like name and status.

    Built a view page showing a list of all allocation groups and their assignments.

    Added the ability to view details of a specific allocation group by selecting it from the list.

    Enabled edit functionality, allowing users to update allocation group details, as long as they have the right permissions.

Impact:
Users now have end-to-end control over allocation groups — from creation to update — directly in the UI, all governed by a permission model.

